{
  "id": "Compound::DB00255 - Gene::1559",
  "verbalization": "Diethylstilbestrol (DES) is implicated in the regulation of Cyp2c9 through a series of molecular interactions involving cytochrome P450 enzymes. The evidence suggests that DES binds to Cyp2c8, which in turn participates in oxidative metabolic pathways, including caffeine oxidase activity and arachidonic acid monooxygenase activity. These activities are ultimately linked to Cyp2c9, indicating a potential functional relationship where DES may influence the expression or activity of Cyp2c9 via its interaction with Cyp2c8. The shared participation of Cyp2c8 in multiple metabolic processes suggests that DES could modulate these pathways, potentially affecting Cyp2c9's role in drug metabolism. The integration of these pathways highlights a possible mechanism by which DES exerts its effects on Cyp2c9, though the exact nature of this interaction remains to be fully elucidated.",
